1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:05,013
A quantum research software engineer turns detector counts into results

2
00:00:05,013 --> 00:00:06,890
a team can defend.

3
00:00:06,890 --> 00:00:09,706
Channel-mapping errors can change those results.

4
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:11,179
Two patches.

5
00:00:11,179 --> 00:00:12,039
Same total.

6
00:00:12,039 --> 00:00:13,328
One is wrong.

7
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:20,367
Here, I run two curated local samples.

8
00:00:20,367 --> 00:00:22,978
Both produce two point six zero.

9
00:00:22,978 --> 00:00:26,025
Only one preserves every registered pair correlation.

10
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:28,637
The deliberately wrong control is rejected.

11
00:00:28,637 --> 00:00:32,990
All study inputs are synthetic, and this browser review makes

12
00:00:32,990 --> 00:00:34,731
no new model call.

13
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:46,548
For the real model step, NVIDIA Nemotron ran on Nebius Token Factory.

14
00:00:46,548 --> 00:00:50,034
Our prompt supplied the declared A-one channel convention.

15
00:00:50,034 --> 00:00:54,391
The model translated it into two parameter arrays; it did

16
00:00:54,391 --> 00:00:56,134
not discover the correction.

17
00:00:56,134 --> 00:01:01,798
A deterministic adapter built the patch, while protected counts and tests stayed fixed.

18
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:15,474
A separate recorded Nebius Sandbox run tested three variants against unchanged protected tests.

19
00:01:15,474 --> 00:01:16,894
The baseline failed.

20
00:01:16,894 --> 00:01:20,208
The NVIDIA repair passed all four checks.

21
00:01:20,208 --> 00:01:22,575
The wrong-pair control was rejected.

22
00:01:22,575 --> 00:01:27,308
The disposable operation took one point two seven three seconds,

23
00:01:27,308 --> 00:01:29,202
with guest networking disabled.

24
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:35,737
The repaired analysis computes two point six zero.

25
00:01:35,737 --> 00:01:39,155
The original claim was three point four zero.

26
00:01:39,155 --> 00:01:43,000
Passing the code checks does not reproduce that claim.

27
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,271
LabRepair keeps both decisions separate, so accepting a repair cannot

28
00:01:47,271 --> 00:01:49,407
silently approve the scientific conclusion.

29
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:56,876
Now I select the incomplete-evidence sample.

30
00:01:56,876 --> 00:02:01,561
This local control asks for review instead of inventing missing values.

31
00:02:01,561 --> 00:02:05,394
It was not part of the recorded cloud run.

32
00:02:05,394 --> 00:02:07,098
Unknown evidence stays unknown.

33
00:02:11,320 --> 00:02:15,729
The researcher records a hold against the reviewed source and

34
00:02:15,729 --> 00:02:17,492
downloads its evidence receipt.

35
00:02:17,492 --> 00:02:21,019
The handover preserves checks, reasons and source bindings.

36
00:02:21,019 --> 00:02:25,869
Review intent launches no job and leaves the original claim unchanged.

37
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,975
Code repair: passed.

38
00:02:30,975 --> 00:02:33,182
Original claim: not reproduced.

39
00:02:33,182 --> 00:02:33,734
LabRepair.

40
00:02:33,734 --> 00:02:35,389
Repair the analysis.

41
00:02:35,389 --> 00:02:37,044
Preserve the evidence.
